<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="c2e32cda-bfc6-536a-af06-a37aa3e38d7b" activityNameId="83de1fdd-6166-5c2f-9b74-046cb9d50b65" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Diesel, burned in building machine, average</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Diesel, burned in building machine, average
The average service life (10'000 h/p) and the consumption of lubricating oil are taken from ecoinvent v2.2. Fuel consumption and regulated exhaust emissions are calculated with the non-road database published by BAFU (2015) for 2015. Data from the Emissions Inventory Guidebook (EMEP/EEA, 2013) were used for specific exhaust emissions not covered by the non-road database. Average emission factors for building machines with and without particle filter were used. The NMVOC speciation was modelled by the shares for lorries and the noise emissions were assumed to be proportional to the fuel consumption of lorries. The fuel consumption of average lorries was calculated with the HBEFA database with data for Switzerland in 2015.;
UUID: e4e7ddc0-f7d1-3fad-bd12-9d6981142800
This dataset represents the combustion of 1 MJ Diesel fuel in an average building machine in Switzerland. A wide range of different building machines is included but hydraulic diggers, pumps and mobile power generators are not considered. The dataset refers to the entire transport life cycle i.e. to the production, operation, maintenance and end of life of vehicle.
Location: Switzerland
Technology: Diesel and diesel engine
Time period: Time of publications
Production volume: na
Sampling: Statistics 
Extrapolations: Noise emissions and NMVOC speciation modelled based on data for lorries.
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_e4e7ddc0-f7d1-3fad-bd12-9d6981142800.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
